20260716 miner_1 lead-lag cycle: explored leave-one-out peer-median five-day return as an orthogonal cross-asset signal. Across all 15 tradable assets and 2020-01-01 through 2026-07-15, 995 daily cross-sectional observations averaged 14.37 valid instruments. Peer-median lead-lag produced daily paper IC .05643, ICIR .17343, hit ratio .5578, coverage 95.78%, and rank turnover approximately .2259; decay was 5d IC .04298/ICIR .12325 and 10d IC .02043/ICIR .06106. Maximum absolute library correlation was .4091 (with existing 5d reversal; -0.2364 with 3d reversal and .1777 with risk-adjusted momentum), below the .5 redundancy gate. Persisted as factors/miner_1_20260716_peer_median_leadlag_5d.json with EFFECTIVE status and explicit validation.metrics.max_abs_library_correlation=.4091. No orders or holdings; warm-up account remains frozen. factor_ensemble not changed by Miner. Future work: revalidate in later regimes and assess adding this short-horizon signal to the ensemble without over-weighting the correlated reversal cluster.
20260716 strategy update: activated 3-factor ensemble (peer lead-lag 39.5%, 5d reversal 30.5%, risk-adjusted momentum 30.0%), 60% signal rank plus 40% inverse-vol, 10-day rebalance, bearish defensive tilt XAU/US10Y/CN10Y. Backtest 30d +0.42% return, Sharpe 0.49, max drawdown 1.36%; 60d +1.78%, Sharpe 0.56, max drawdown 6.15%. Fixed fractional-order validation bug using integer quantities. Warm-up step disabled; no live PnL, turnover, or slippage.
20260716 miner_1 conditional q75 reversal cycle: explored 3-day reversal gated to lowest-volatility 75% cross-section (15 assets, 2,388 dates, 2020-01-01 through 2026-07-15). It cleared paper IC 0.03896 and ICIR 0.09845 (1d; 1,819 observations, mean valid N 11.0), but coverage was 72.99% and rank turnover 0.7867. Five-day IC 0.02313/ICIR 0.05728 and ten-day 0.01775/0.04428; late 5d IC decayed to 0.01221. Pooled correlations with library proxies were 0.775 with short_term_reversal_5d, 1.000 with 3d reversal (unmasked), -0.363 with risk-adjusted momentum, and -0.022 with peer lead-lag; max library correlation therefore exceeds 0.5 and candidate was rejected for redundancy/high turnover. No factor persisted; ensemble unchanged. Continue seeking orthogonal, lower-turnover regime or cross-asset factors and revalidate existing library.

