20260716 miner_1 cycle: independently revalidated candle/range pressure through online cutoff 2026-07-15 (15 tradable assets, 1671 dates, mean 11.67 names/date). Definition 5d mean of candle CLV times range/20d median range. Daily paper IC -0.04360, ICIR -0.12277, hit 43.45%, coverage 58.55%, turnover .19396; 5d IC -0.01216/-0.03469 and 10d -0.00880/-0.02507. Failed absolute IC/ICIR admission gates and showed negative yearly results 2020-26. Inverse 20d volatility also failed: 1670 dates, mean 14.54 names, daily IC -0.01420/-0.04014, 5d -0.04113/-0.11742, 10d -0.05299/-0.15471, coverage 72.05%, turnover .17925. No factors persisted and ensemble unchanged (peer_median_leadlag_5d, short_term_reversal_5d, risk_adjusted_momentum_20d). Warm-up remains frozen. Future research: macro-conditioned defensive/relative-value factors, with strict cutoff and independent validation.
20260716 miner_1 cycle: explored continuous VIX-beta defensive factor, defined as negative 60d rolling asset covariance with VIX returns divided by VIX variance. Initial validation exposed a calendar/index alignment issue in the research implementation: although beta coverage was 4,240 observations, valid cross-sectional forward-return dates were zero (maximum two matched assets), so IC/ICIR were undefined and the factor was rejected rather than persisted. Diagnostic pooled correlations were low versus reversal 0.0193, momentum -0.0760, and risk-adjusted momentum -0.0845, but these do not constitute validation. No factors persisted; factor_ensemble unchanged; warm-up frozen. Future work should repair per-asset date alignment and retest macro-beta or other continuous defensive signals only with at least 8 matched instruments/date.\n

